AIM: Set up navigation between different screens using navigator
DESCRIPTION:
Navigation is a fundamental part of mobile app development where users move from one 
screen (page) to another. Flutter provides a built-in Navigator widget that manages a stack￾based navigation system.
• When a new screen is opened, it is pushed onto the stack.
• When returning to the previous screen, it is popped from the stack.
Flutter supports two types of navigation:
1. Navigator.push() / Navigator.pop() — Direct stack-based navigation
2. Named Routes — Structured navigation using route names (for better scalability)
In this experiment, we create multiple screens and navigate between them using buttons. We 
also explore how screens are added and removed from the navigation stack to maintain the 
correct flow of the app.
PROGRAM:
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
void main() {
 runApp(MyApp());
}
class MyApp extends StatelessWidget {
 @override
 Widget build(BuildContext context) {
 return MaterialApp(
 title: 'Flutter Navigation Demo',
 theme: ThemeData(primarySwatch: Colors.blue),
 home: HomeScreen(), // starting screen
 );
 }
}
// First Screen
class HomeScreen extends StatelessWidget {
 @override
 Widget build(BuildContext context) {
 return Scaffold(
 appBar: AppBar(title: Text("Home Screen")),
 body: Center(
 child: ElevatedButton(
 child: Text("Go to Second Screen"),
 onPressed: () {
 // Navigate to SecondScreen
 Navigator.push(
 context,
 MaterialPageRoute(builder: (context) => SecondScreen()),
 );
 },
 ),
 ),
 );
 }
}
// Second Screen (Row & Column with clear matter)
class SecondScreen extends StatelessWidget {
 @override
 Widget build(BuildContext context) {
 return Scaffold(
 appBar: AppBar(title: Text("Second Screen")),
 body: Padding(
 padding: const EdgeInsets.all(20.0),
 child: Column(
 mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.start,
 children: [
 Text(
 "Understanding Column Widget",
 style: TextStyle(fontSize: 22, fontWeight: FontWeight.bold),
 ),
 SizedBox(height: 10),
 Text(
 "➡ Column arranges widgets vertically (from top to bottom).",
 style: TextStyle(fontSize: 16),
 ),
 SizedBox(height: 30),
 Text(
 "Understanding Row Widget",
 style: TextStyle(fontSize: 22, fontWeight: FontWeight.bold),
 ),
 SizedBox(height: 10),
 Row(
 mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.center,
 children: [
 Icon(Icons.arrow_forward, color: Colors.blue, size: 30),
 SizedBox(width: 10),
 Text(
 "Row arranges widgets horizontally (side by side).",
 style: TextStyle(fontSize: 16),
 ),
 ],
 ),
 ],
 ),
 ),
 );
 }
}
